   "versionNonce": 536574445,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1748000000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Round 1 detail: 1->2 gives 6, then 3->2 (7-2=5)\nIMPROVES it to 5 \u2014 negative edges flip the 'obvious' route.\nBest route to 2 is 1->3->2, not the direct edge!\n\nNegative cycle example: 1->2 (1), 2->3 (-3), 3->1 (1)\nloop cost = -1 -> dist[1] keeps decreasing ->\nverification pass still improves -> print -1.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "originalText": "Round 1 detail: 1->2 gives 6, then 3->2 (7-2=5)\nIMPROVES it to 5 \u2014 negative edges flip the 'obvious' route.\nBest route to 2 is 1->3->2, not the direct edge!\n\nNegative cycle example: 1->2 (1), 2->3 (-3), 3->1 (1)\nloop cost = -1 -> dist[1] keeps decreasing ->\nverification pass still improves -> print -1.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
